The changed line adds a `web_download=True` filter to a `CachedFile` lookup by a user-supplied id. The `CachedFile` model has no owner/organizer/event field — it is a global table keyed by UUID, and the only access-control mechanism is `web_download` plus an optional `session_key`. The PR change does not add any ownership or session check; it merely narrows the set of files to those marked web-downloadable. The view itself is protected by `EventPermissionRequiredMixin` with `can_change_settings`, but that only gates the endpoint, not the specific object. This is a pre-existing IDOR pattern (any user with the permission on any event can reference any `web_download=True` CachedFile by id), and the PR does not newly introduce or expose it — it only tightens the filter. No new authorization flaw is introduced by this change.

